{"name":"Merlin’s Cloak","hex":"#89556e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"merlin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small falcon, Falco columbarius, that breeds in northern North America, Europe, and Asia."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cytoskeletal protein active in the suppression of tumors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merlin"},{"term":"cloak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long outer garment worn over the shoulders covering the back; a cape, often with a hood.","A blanket-like covering, often metaphorical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover as with or like a cloak.","To cover up, hide or conceal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloak","blocks":[{"text":"A cloak is a type of loose garment worn over clothing, mostly but not always, as outerwear for outdoor wear, which serves the same purpose as an overcoat and protects the wearer from the weather. It may form part of a uniform. People in many different societies may wear cloaks. Over time, cloak designs have changed to match fashion and available textiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg/330px-Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak","wikidata":"Q516992"},{"title":"Merlin","blocks":[{"text":"Merlin is a mythical figure prominently featured in the legend of King Arthur and best known as a prophet and a magician, along with several other main roles. The familiar depiction of Merlin, based on an amalgamation of historical and legendary figures, was introduced by the 12th-century Catholic cleric Geoffrey of Monmouth and then built on by the French poet Robert de Boron and prose successors in the 13th century. Geoffrey's account presented Merlin as a prophet and royal advisor to Arthur's father, Uther Pendragon."}]